  "body": "Found during #4336 (U10 of #3663).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe tool editor in the tool library window shows the tool's name as a read-only row. No command renames a tool. Operations, scripts and the MCP tools address a tool by its name, so a typed name that does not land would break the rule \"every edit is an undoable command\".\n\n## Expected\n\n- A command `RenameTool { from, to }` renames the tool and each reference to it (operations, holders by tool, recipes copies) as one undo step.\n- The command refuses an empty name and a name that another tool has, by name.\n- The MCP tool `rename_tool` calls the same command.\n- The Name row of the tool editor becomes a text field. The footer's Apply lands the new name with the other draft fields.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: a rename lands and undoes; references follow the new name; a clash and an empty name are refused by name; the MCP tool calls the same command.\n",
